From 35fe1cfce3a0f47b733a4074470eecdc2123f5e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): pickup window skips cards the local
 pacing governor would hold

Why: worker-6 (11-15 06:35Z) took the top 9 hub cards by admission order every ~16 s. Those were
openai-codex cards held by pacing (limit 1, running 2 to 8). Pickup copied them, local dispatch held
them, and t_294f467cbaa293e4 (anthropic pin, rank 16) was never offered to any worker.

Five whys: card stayed ready -> no worker claimed it -> never inside any worker's 9-card window ->
the window was filled by paced cards -> pickup judged labels and quota walls before spending budget
but not the pacing governor (kanban.llm_pacing), which only ran at claim time after the copy.

Fix: _evaluate asks kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.pickup_hold (read-only twin of hold, same resolver,
same pace, this machine's running count) for each otherwise-eligible card. A held card is skipped
(pickup skip "other", llm_paced) and takes no budget, so the window fills with the next runnable
cards in admission order and stays bounded by the same budget. It is offered again on the tick its
limit frees. Any fault copies as before (fail open; local dispatch still decides).

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_paced_window.py. RED on origin/main (3 of 4 fail: 9 paced
codex copies, anthropic card not offered), GREEN with the change: 12 paced codex cards ahead of one
anthropic card, that card is picked in one poll; window bounded and ordered; paced card offered when
its pool opens; failed check copies as before.
